        body: 'A woman running a session at a church hall asked everybody to write down the last big money decision they had made in a hurry, and then who they had ASKED before making it — not told afterwards, asked before. She said the room went quiet in a way she had not expected. One man said afterwards that he had written "nobody" and had sat looking at the word for a while. He said he had told four people about it within a week of doing it, and every one of them had been supportive, and it had felt like counsel, and it had not been counsel at all — it had been an audience. He said he did not think any of the four would have stopped him if he had asked first. He said that was not the point. The point was that he had never given them the chance, and that he had constructed a version of his own life where nothing he decided ever had to survive contact with another person, and he had thought of that as independence right up until he wrote the word down.',
